\",\"source-context.md:12-21\",\"spec.json:/full_target\",\"spec.json:/hypotheses\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/P/statement\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/2/text\"]},\"definition_reviews\":{},\"source_reviews\":{\"M001\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The full-signature evidence gives the theorem’s implicit EMetricSpace, MeasurableSpace and BorelSpace instances, Set argument and NNReal exponent; its conclusion is Hausdorff measure = top under ↑d < dimH. This agrees with the official pinned declaration and its surrounding characteristic-property discussion. Probe reports theorem kind and axioms propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound, and the commit/path/hash match the candidate. In the stated application, E is the subset of Euclidean space, s is positive and below dim_H(E), and d is its NNReal exponent, so the strict-inequality premise is the one needed. This source review does not validate other unsupported steps in R001.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M001/0/sources/M001/signature\",\"signature-evidence.json:/M001/0/sources/M001/axioms\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/1/source\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/0\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:94-98\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:105-118\"]},\"M002\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The full-signature evidence states the countable-index and per-index AEMeasurable hypotheses and the ENNReal lintegral/tsum equality. The official pinned declaration agrees; its [Countable β] instance is visible in the declaration, and its proof is the countable-sum monotone-convergence argument. In the candidate application β=ℕ is countable and the proposed summands are nonnegative ENNReal indicators times constants; measurability is asserted for Borel intervals on restricted Lebesgue measure. The source theorem itself is faithfully stated and is suitable for that claimed use, conditional on the summands’ AEMeasurability. This does not supply the other measure/content calculations left unproved in R001.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M002/0/sources/M002/signature\",\"signature-evidence.json:/M002/0/sources/M002/axioms\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/2/source\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/1\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Integral/Lebesgue/Add.lean:27-28\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Integral/Lebesgue/Add.lean:360-369\"]}},\"structure_review\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The visible graph has a single producer R001 for P, both H nodes and both M nodes are direct inputs, and there is no extra hypothesis or additional target. Its one inference is nevertheless not a valid AND-closed proof: the R body invokes undeclared mathematical results and unproved nontrivial measure/dimension implications. Consequently the required mathematical acceptance of the sole inference fails, so P is not reached by A3 AND closure. No packet replay is claimed.\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:/propositions\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/inputs\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/output\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/1/text\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/2/text\"]},\"findings\":[{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"location\":\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/2/text\",\"finding\":\"S003 applies the general Lipschitz-image dimension inequality and Real.dimH_of_nonempty_interior to establish the lower bound when D=0, but neither result is an M/E input, definition, nor proved earlier in the graph. The inference from the stated premises to dim_H(F)≥1 is unsupported under the declared source policy.\"},{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"location\":\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/0/text\",\"finding\":\"S001 uses the Hausdorff-dimension threshold implication H^q(E)=0 for q>D, the scale-content characterization, and the consequence that zero Hausdorff measure gives dim_H(F)≤q+1. These are not among the graph inputs; the text's invocation of a 'definition' does not establish all of these substantive threshold properties. The asserted upper bound is therefore not closed relative to the declared inputs.\"},{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"location\":\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/1/text\",\"finding\":\"S002 asserts the exact scale-content formula for H^a, divergence of content from M001's infinite-measure conclusion, comparison of content infima, the indicator integral/interval-length calculation, and the dimension consequence s+1≤dim_H(F), without declaring or proving all required Hausdorff-measure and Lebesgue-measure facts. M001 and M002 alone do not establish these steps.\"},{\"severity\":\"scope\",\"location\":\"problem.md:3; frozen-target.md:3-17; source-context.md:12-21\",\"finding\":\"The raw exercise says compact E and does not exclude E=∅; the equality is false for E=∅ with dim_H(∅)=0. The frozen target explicitly records the user-approved nonempty strengthening, so the spec correctly audits that approved target rather than claiming fidelity to the literal unstrengthened exercise.\"}]}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"funct